**Issue**: The port is hardcoded to `3000` in two places.

**Security & Deployability Concerns**:
- Port 3000 might not be available in all environments
- Different environments (dev, staging, prod) typically use different ports
- Cloud platforms often assign ports dynamically via environment variables
- Hardcoded ports can cause conflicts when running multiple instances

**Recommendation**:
```javascript
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
});
```

